                        <p></p><h2>
	Book Itinerary</h2>
<p>
	A saved itinerary can be confirmed at a later time. In order to do this yo=
u must use the bookitinerary command.</p>
<p>
	<strong>The confirmation of a saved itinerary is a process made in two ste=
ps.</strong> After the first step (bookitinerary <strong>with confirm no</s=
trong>) the system will return the corresponding details of each service of=
 the itinerary - if it can be booked, the actual prices, etc. The second st=
ep requires another bookitinerary request that specifies the confirmation (=
<strong>confirm yes</strong>).</p>
<div>
	For <strong>credit</strong> <strong>card customers</strong> the confirmati=
on of a saved itinerary is a three steps process. Like for the credit clien=
ts, in the first step (<strong>bookitinerary with confirm=3Dno</strong>) ou=
r system will return the corresponding details of each service of the itine=
rary.&nbsp;</div>
<div>
	The second step of the confirmation process (<strong>bookitinerary with co=
nfirm=3Dpreauth</strong>) will authorize the transaction with the credit ca=
rd processor and the xml response will indicate if the transaction will be =
3DS or non-3DS.</div>
<div>
	By posting the the third step (<strong>bookitinerary with confirm=3Dyes</s=
trong>) the reservation will be finalized. The complete credit card payment=
 flow is detailed at <strong>Credit card payment</strong> section.</div>
<h3>
	General Request</h3>
