                        <p></p><h1>
	Re-confirm booking process</h1>
<p>
	The new feature has the purpose to enhance our customers experience, by pr=
oviding alternative offers in cases when DOTW receive from its suppliers di=
fferent conditions in the confirmation step.<brthe br=3D"" can=3D"" cancell=
ation=3D"" conditions=3D"" imply=3D"" new=3D"" or=3D"" policy=3D"" price=3D=
""><br>
	Therefore, instead of only returning an error message in such cases, the r=
e-confirmation process will provide additional details about the new bookin=
g conditions, offering to our customers the possibility to finalize the boo=
king.<br>
	<br>
	The bookItinerary response will still return an error Code and error messa=
ge, but in addition to this, the extraDetails tag will contain the new book=
ing conditions.</brthe></p>
<p>
	<brthe br=3D"" can=3D"" cancellation=3D"" conditions=3D"" imply=3D"" new=
=3D"" or=3D"" policy=3D"" price=3D""><b>important:</b> For those customers =
who are interested to implement the re-confirmation process logic, it is ma=
ndatory to add in the bookItinerary request a new tag: &lt;</brthe><brthe b=
r=3D"" can=3D"" cancellation=3D"" conditions=3D"" imply=3D"" new=3D"" or=3D=
"" policy=3D"" price=3D""><span><span class=3D"tag-name">returnReconfirm</s=
pan></span>&gt;. Additional details can be found under Hotel Comm Structure=
 -&gt; BookItinerary -&gt; General Request section.<br>
	</brthe></p>
<p>
	It is mandatory that in the new bookItinerary request, the customer will u=
se the <b>allocationDetails</b> token generated in the extraDetails tag, as=
 this encapsulates the new booking conditions.</p>
<p></p>
